  "title": "Jericallas (Mexican Baked Custards)",
  "description": "Jericallas, a vanilla-flavored flan from the Mexican city of Guadalajara was, according to legend, invented by nuns in the 19th century.",
  "authors": [
    "CeciliaR"
  ],
